From 234f7bc1461a4c68f642228811b25a9334ee87fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:59:24 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] PlaitOS: Cut and Copy use Files' own clipboard, not the
 system one

PlaitClipboard holds the cut/copied documents for the Files process (all Files windows
share it), with ClipboardManager's calls, so RuntimeDocumentClipper and everything on it
(the Paste here bar, Paste in the menu, paste into a folder, clearing after a move) work
unchanged. Nothing reaches the system clipboard: no "Copied" overlay, other apps don't see
the file list, and copying text elsewhere doesn't drop it. The "added to clipboard"
snackbar is gone too (the Paste here bar says what is waiting).

Checked on the phone: copy two files Download > Documents, cut them Documents > a folder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017VXjYUWzBqMCeUoJD2Suc4
